A SQLite worker commits the operation ledger insert and counter increment in one transaction. The ledger operation ID is a database-enforced PRIMARY KEY. The same operation ID is redelivered once after the first commit is not acknowledged.

Measured local trace:
{"deliveries": [{"action": "effect_committed", "attempt": 1, "effect_count": 1, "operation_id": "operation-1"}, {"action": "duplicate_rejected_by_unique_constraint", "attempt": 2, "effect_count": 1, "operation_id": "operation-1"}], "effect_count": 1, "failure_injection": "First commit's queue acknowledgement is withheld; the same ID is redelivered. This retry schedule is simulated; no process is killed in this scenario.", "ledger_rows": 1, "operation_id_reused": true}

A SQLite worker commits the operation ledger insert and counter increment in one transaction. The ledger operation ID is an ordinary column with no uniqueness constraint. The same operation ID is redelivered once after the first commit is not acknowledged.

Measured local trace:
{"deliveries": [{"action": "effect_committed", "attempt": 1, "effect_count": 1, "operation_id": "operation-1"}, {"action": "effect_committed", "attempt": 2, "effect_count": 2, "operation_id": "operation-1"}], "effect_count": 2, "failure_injection": "First commit's queue acknowledgement is withheld; the same ID is redelivered. This retry schedule is simulated; no process is killed in this scenario.", "ledger_rows": 2, "operation_id_reused": true}

A SQLite writer inserts one append using a DELETE journal and synchronous=FULL. It commits before emitting success. Immediately after emitting success, the writer process exits abruptly without cleanup.

Measured local trace:
{"acknowledgement": {"commit_before_ack": true, "event": "acknowledged", "operation_id": "append-1"}, "child_exit_code": 73, "failure_scope": "writer_process_only", "journal_mode": "DELETE", "persisted_after_process_exit": ["append-1"], "synchronous": "FULL"}

A SQLite writer inserts one append using a DELETE journal and synchronous=FULL. It emits success while the insert transaction is still uncommitted. Immediately after emitting success, the writer process exits abruptly without cleanup.

Measured local trace:
{"acknowledgement": {"commit_before_ack": false, "event": "acknowledged", "operation_id": "append-1"}, "child_exit_code": 73, "failure_scope": "writer_process_only", "journal_mode": "DELETE", "persisted_after_process_exit": [], "synchronous": "FULL"}

Three messages arrive while no consumer runs. The ingress uses queue.Queue(maxsize=2) and rejects a put_nowait call that raises Full, before telling its producer the message was accepted.

Measured local trace:
{"accepted": ["message-1", "message-2"], "arrivals": ["message-1", "message-2", "message-3"], "capacity": 2, "consumer_ran_during_burst": false, "depth_after_each_arrival": [1, 2, 2], "missing_accepted_messages": [], "rejected_before_accept": ["message-3"], "retained_before_consumption": ["message-1", "message-2"]}

Three messages arrive while no consumer runs. The ingress uses deque(maxlen=2) and tells every producer its message was accepted. Appending a third message silently evicts the oldest queued item.

Measured local trace:
{"accepted": ["message-1", "message-2", "message-3"], "arrivals": ["message-1", "message-2", "message-3"], "capacity": 2, "consumer_ran_during_burst": false, "depth_after_each_arrival": [1, 2, 2], "missing_accepted_messages": ["message-1"], "rejected_before_accept": [], "retained_before_consumption": ["message-2", "message-3"]}

A SQLite handler transfers 10 units by debiting one account and crediting another. Both updates share one explicit transaction. Failure between writes triggers rollback. A separate connection reads balances between the writes and again after the failure.

Measured local trace:
{"failure_injection": "Explicit exception between debit and credit; not a process/host crash", "independent_reader_after_failure": [100, 0], "independent_reader_between_writes": [100, 0], "original_balances": [100, 0], "successful_full_transfer": [90, 10]}

A SQLite handler transfers 10 units by debiting one account and crediting another. Each update commits independently. Failure after debit leaves that commit in place. A separate connection reads balances between the writes and again after the failure.

Measured local trace:
